{
  "_README": [
    "The list of every feed the Gospel News Access wire reads.",
    "",
    "HOW TO READ AN ENTRY:",
    "  tier 1 = breaking, polled every 30 minutes (Google News topic queries)",
    "  tier 2 = established faith outlets, polled hourly",
    "  tier 3 = gospel and Christian music trade press, polled hourly",
    "",
    "THE VERIFICATION RULE — this is a safety mechanism, not paperwork:",
    "  A source is used ONLY when \"status\" reads \"verified\".",
    "  scripts/wire.py SKIPS every source that is not verified, so an",
    "  unchecked or dead URL can never put a story on the live site.",
    "",
    "  scripts/verify_feeds.py is what flips the switch. It fetches the URL,",
    "  confirms the response is valid XML, confirms it contains items dated",
    "  within the last 30 days, then records the date it checked in",
    "  \"verified\". If the main url fails it tries each entry in",
    "  \"url_candidates\" and promotes whichever one actually works.",
    "",
    "  Verification runs on GitHub Actions (.github/workflows/verify-feeds.yml)",
    "  because that runner has open internet access.",
    "",
    "A feed that returns zero items twice in a row is logged to",
    "data/feed-health.json so a quietly dead source cannot hide."
  ],
